  "claim_boundary": "V1 times the same NVFP4 up_proj GEMV kernel on the same bytes, once from device memory and once through a UVA pointer into the pinned host bank. It is a feasibility number for a device-side router that would service misses from host, NOT a router and NOT a token time; the budget it is compared against is arithmetic on Y1's measured sync cost and K0's measured miss rate. W1-R1 is a paired design: each triplet's effect is the fast step against the mean of its two neighbouring base steps, which removes a thermal trend but not per-step noise. The adoption gate G-W1-P1 is unchanged at 1.0 ms."
